From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FIX-23: show agents' average FAQ rating on the FAQs admin page

Adds an "Agent rating" column (average out of 5 and the rating count) to the
Knowledge > FAQs table. The numbers come from GET /kb/faq, which now returns
`avg_score` and `rating_count` per entry; the ratings themselves are posted
from the composer strip (patch 0056). Unrated FAQs show a dash. A separate
patch (not an edit of 0010/0040) so the earlier KnowledgeFaqs.vue patches keep
their context untouched.
---
diff --git a/app/javascript/dashboard/components/proton/KnowledgeFaqs.vue b/app/javascript/dashboard/components/proton/KnowledgeFaqs.vue
index 238975c..0f2f0c2 100644
--- a/app/javascript/dashboard/components/proton/KnowledgeFaqs.vue
+++ b/app/javascript/dashboard/components/proton/KnowledgeFaqs.vue
@@ -253,6 +253,9 @@ onMounted(load);
               <th class="px-3 py-2 font-medium text-n-slate-11">Keywords</th>
               <th class="px-3 py-2 font-medium text-n-slate-11">Tags</th>
               <th class="px-3 py-2 font-medium text-n-slate-11">Active</th>
+              <th class="px-3 py-2 font-medium text-n-slate-11">
+                Agent rating
+              </th>
               <th class="px-3 py-2 font-medium text-n-slate-11">Actions</th>
             </tr>
           </thead>
@@ -291,6 +294,14 @@ onMounted(load);
               <td class="px-3 py-2 text-n-slate-11">
                 {{ entry.active === false ? 'no' : 'yes' }}
               </td>
+              <td class="px-3 py-2 text-n-slate-11 whitespace-nowrap">
+                <!-- FIX-23: 1-5 average of agents' thumbs (up = 5, down = 1). -->
+                <span v-if="entry.rating_count">
+                  {{ entry.avg_score }} / 5
+                  <span class="text-n-slate-10">({{ entry.rating_count }})</span>
+                </span>
+                <span v-else class="text-n-slate-10">—</span>
+              </td>
               <td class="px-3 py-2 whitespace-nowrap">
                 <button
                   class="mr-2 text-xs text-n-brand hover:underline"
